    "id": "rate_half_list_budget_three_fiber_two_cycle_c2_parity_trace_jacobi_router",
    "title": "Budget-three fiber-two c=2 parity has three traces and shares the CR-002 Jacobi norms",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On a two-antipodal c=2 denominator, normalize the roots to {1,-1,r,-r} and put tau=r^2. The exact primary/secondary packet is the existing univariate parity system at M=2^36. The six selected denominator pairs collapse to trace classes 0, 2+r+r^-1, and 2-r-r^-1, each twice; completion coupling is J_out=0 or the orientation-free product of the outer invariant cubic at the latter two traces. Every survivor also passes the same degree-2^36 Jacobi primary/torsion gcd and CR-002 norm pair used by matched c=0 and generic c=1 parity. This does not force general denominators to be parity or evaluate the norms.",
